From f07e8a2b135f59b32492c312ef35f56831dfe8a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 05:13:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] MUMPSSolver: ReuseAnalysis parameter

The analysis of MUMPS (ordering and symbolic factorization) is redone for
each new matrix, although the matrices of the successive iterations of the
non linear solvers usually have the same pattern. With the new parameter
ReuseAnalysis (false by default), the analysis of the previous matrix is
reused when the pattern of the local part of the new one (rows, column
indices of the diagonal and off-diagonal blocks, global indices of the
off-diagonal columns) is the same on all processes.
mfem::MUMPSSolver::SetReorderingReuse (MFEM 4.10) does not check the
pattern, which is why it is compared here, and the analysis being
collective, a new one is made on all processes if the pattern changed on
one of them.

On the elasticity matrix of ex8 of mfem-mgis-examples (28548 unknowns),
each factorization takes 0.206 s with the reuse instead of 0.256 s on
one process, and 0.137 s instead of 0.19 s on two. The ordering
strategies and the block low-rank factorization of MUMPS give no gain on
this matrix.

The test MUMPSReuseAnalysisTest checks the solutions of a sequence of
matrices whose pattern is kept, changes on all processes, changes on the
last process only, or only changes by the column indices of the
off-diagonal blocks, on one and two processes, with and without the
reuse, for symmetric and non symmetric matrices.
